    body = phrase {
        payload = "RecurLoop represents names, values and language constructs through phrases. Ordinary programs use the standard vocabulary; libraries can add functions, data structures and new syntax to the same language environment.

## Begin here

[Install the RecurLoop binary](installation.rl) for terminal use, or [set up the VS Code extension](installation-vscode.rl). Then write your [First program](first-program.rl) and create your [First project](first-project.rl), including tasks, a project console and F5 debugging in VS Code.

## Follow the learning path

[The learning path](language.rl) leads from values and control flow to typed functions, records, phrases, syntax extensions and native output. The sidebar and Previous/Next links follow that sequence.

## Learn an application vocabulary

Use [Libraries](libraries.rl) to choose a standard vocabulary. Its overview introduces the purpose and first example; later chapters explain each capability and its ownership rules. The API section provides exact names and contracts.

## Use the two levels of navigation

The sidebar lists broad topics. On this page lists the detailed questions answered within the current topic. Search covers both guides and phrase references."
    }
